1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,550
The page model, and the tree.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:07,191
Last episode we made a prediction.

3
00:00:07,191 --> 00:00:12,706
A page one level under Home would get the path zero zero zero one,

4
00:00:12,706 --> 00:00:15,965
zero zero zero one, zero zero zero one.

5
00:00:15,965 --> 00:00:19,224
Today we build that page, and we check.

6
00:00:20,024 --> 00:00:22,960
Here is where we left the home page.

7
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:29,158
Two lines, and already a working page type, because Page brings title, slug,

8
00:00:29,158 --> 00:00:33,235
SEO fields, publishing, revisions and permissions.

9
00:00:33,235 --> 00:00:36,661
What it does not have is anything of ours.

10
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:38,210
So let us add some.

11
00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:39,874
Two fields.

12
00:00:39,874 --> 00:00:42,936
Intro is an ordinary Django char field,

13
00:00:42,936 --> 00:00:49,060
and the help text is what the editor sees under the box, so write it for them.

14
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:52,515
Body is a rich text field, Wagtail's editor.

15
00:00:52,515 --> 00:00:56,284
And then the part people forget: content panels.

16
00:00:57,084 --> 00:01:01,295
A field on the model is not the same as a field in the admin.

17
00:01:01,295 --> 00:01:05,161
Adding it gives you a database column, and nothing else.

18
00:01:05,161 --> 00:01:08,681
It only becomes editable once it has a field panel.

19
00:01:08,681 --> 00:01:12,823
And we add to Page.content_panels, rather than replacing it,

20
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:16,758
so we keep the title field that Wagtail already provides.

21
00:01:17,558 --> 00:01:19,516
And a second page type.

22
00:01:19,516 --> 00:01:25,135
Standard page, for About, Services, anything that is mostly words.

23
00:01:25,135 --> 00:01:26,497
Same two fields.

24
00:01:26,497 --> 00:01:31,520
Having two page types is what lets us build an actual tree.

25
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:34,838
Every page type needs a template,

26
00:01:34,838 --> 00:01:39,111
named by the rule from last episode: standard_page.html.

27
00:01:39,111 --> 00:01:45,368
Leave it out and you get template does not exist, but only when you hit view live,

28
00:01:45,368 --> 00:01:50,023
so the admin looks perfectly fine right up until you preview.

29
00:01:50,023 --> 00:01:52,083
We keep this template bare.

30
00:01:52,083 --> 00:01:53,914
Styling is episode four.

31
00:01:54,714 --> 00:01:56,833
Make the migration.

32
00:01:56,833 --> 00:02:00,179
One new model, two new fields.

33
00:02:00,179 --> 00:02:01,740
Then apply it.

34
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:09,282
Now open that migration, because one line in it explains how every Wagtail page is

35
00:02:09,282 --> 00:02:09,858
stored.

36
00:02:09,858 --> 00:02:10,927
Page pointer.

37
00:02:10,927 --> 00:02:15,038
A one to one field, pointing at wagtail core page.

38
00:02:15,838 --> 00:02:18,939
That is Django multi table inheritance,

39
00:02:18,939 --> 00:02:23,312
and it is the mental model for the rest of this series.

40
00:02:23,312 --> 00:02:25,777
Every page lives in two tables.

41
00:02:25,777 --> 00:02:31,501
The shared page table has twenty nine columns: title, slug, path, depth,

42
00:02:31,501 --> 00:02:34,602
and the content type from last episode.

43
00:02:34,602 --> 00:02:37,305
Our standard page table has three.

44
00:02:37,305 --> 00:02:39,690
Page pointer, intro, and body.

45
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:42,712
Only what is unique to this page type.

46
00:02:42,712 --> 00:02:45,256
Page pointer is what joins them.

47
00:02:46,056 --> 00:02:47,410
Over to the admin.

48
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:53,729
Edit the home page, and there are the two new fields, with our help text underneath.

49
00:02:53,729 --> 00:02:55,986
Fill in the intro and publish.

50
00:02:56,786 --> 00:02:59,302
Now on Home, add a child page.

51
00:02:59,302 --> 00:03:04,418
Choose standard page, call it About, fill it in, and publish.

52
00:03:04,418 --> 00:03:08,276
That is our first page that we made ourselves.

53
00:03:09,076 --> 00:03:11,308
Now the moment of truth.

54
00:03:11,308 --> 00:03:14,470
Open the shell and print the tree.

55
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:16,353
There it is.

56
00:03:16,353 --> 00:03:22,940
About sits at zero zero zero one, zero zero zero one, zero zero zero one.

57
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:27,451
Exactly what the animation predicted last episode.

58
00:03:27,451 --> 00:03:31,512
It is Home's path, plus four more characters.

59
00:03:32,312 --> 00:03:35,227
But look closely at that url path.

60
00:03:35,227 --> 00:03:36,856
It says/home/about.

61
00:03:36,856 --> 00:03:39,343
Visit that and you get a 404.

62
00:03:39,343 --> 00:03:41,915
The page is actually at/about.

63
00:03:41,915 --> 00:03:48,174
The url path is the route from the root of the tree, so it includes home.

64
00:03:48,174 --> 00:03:54,176
But home is the root of the site, so it drops out of the real address.

65
00:03:54,176 --> 00:03:58,634
If you ever build links, use page.url, not url_path.

66
00:03:59,434 --> 00:04:02,760
And one more thing that catches everyone.

67
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:08,764
Ask Page.objects for About, and you get a plain Page, with no intro field.

68
00:04:08,764 --> 00:04:14,767
Call .specific, and you get the real standard page, with everything on it.

69
00:04:14,767 --> 00:04:17,120
That is the two tables again.

70
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:20,284
Page.objects only reads the shared one.

71
00:04:21,084 --> 00:04:24,338
Before we finish, something is still wrong.

72
00:04:24,338 --> 00:04:29,636
When you add a child under Home, Wagtail offers you Home page as well.

73
00:04:29,636 --> 00:04:33,950
Nothing stops you putting a home page inside a home page.

74
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:37,734
We fix that with sub page types, in episode seven.

75
00:04:38,534 --> 00:04:40,386
Commit it, and tag it.

76
00:04:40,386 --> 00:04:46,448
E p zero three end is our first checkpoint with real code changes in it.

77
00:04:47,248 --> 00:04:53,634
Our pages have content now, but the home page still shows Wagtail's welcome egg.

78
00:04:53,634 --> 00:04:57,466
Next episode, we replace it with real templates.

79
00:04:58,266 --> 00:05:05,222
Next episode, we replace the welcome page with real templates.

80
00:05:05,222 --> 00:05:07,466
Thanks for watching.
